claimed: intent-other-is-a-bin — the consumer request I promised in the room and did not do: Other is not a class, it is a bin. Social pleasantries and support complaints share nothing, so a centroid over them is a point between two clouds belonging to neither, and a probe boundary for it is wherever the mixture happened to fall. Their cheap test first: how much of the centroid gap to the probe lives in Other rows, from output I already have and with no model call. Then the decision the answer forces -- if Other is a REJECTION class it should be scored as abstention rather than as a class, and if it is a class it needs splitting. Every per-class number in this spec was computed with it counted as a class, so the answer reaches back through the whole programme.
